::meta
  title: Core GitHub
  version: 1.0.0
  domain: development|github|issue-tracking

::index
  # node-id    | type  | scope | conf | keywords
  core_github   | skill | all   | 1.0  | github, issue, bug, repo, productivity, pull request, repository, issue tracker, bug report, deploy, deployment, ci, pipeline, devops

::node[core_github]
->[:role=skill]
->[:requires_auth=github_personal_token]
->[:keywords=github, issue, bug, repo, productivity, pull request, repository, issue tracker, bug report, deploy, deployment, ci, pipeline, devops]

::api[create_github_issue]
method=POST
endpoint=https://api.github.com/repos/{owner}/{repo}/issues
headers={"Authorization": "token {github_personal_token}", "Accept": "application/vnd.github.v3+json", "User-Agent": "Hachi-Agent"}
schema={"owner": "string", "repo": "string", "title": "string", "body": "string"}
description=Creates a new issue in a GitHub repository.

::dense
Creates GitHub issues via personal token. Operates on a single designated repository.

::steps
1. Identify the target repository owner, repository name, issue title, and body.
2. If any parameters are missing, politely ask the user to clarify them before proceeding.
3. Call `create_github_issue`.
4. Return the HTML URL of the created issue so the user can click it.

::assertions
assert repo != "" "A target repository name is required."
assert title != "" "An issue title is required."
